    "result": "Perfect! All 28 tests pass now. Let me verify the changes are correct by reviewing what I fixed:\n\n**Issue 1 - governance.test.js**: The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export but it wasn't exported that way. \n- **Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` to the governance module while keeping the default export for backward compatibility.\n\n**Issue 2 - eval/index.test.js**: The `toxicityMetric` function was receiving the references array as its second parameter, which was being interpreted as banned terms, causing false positives.\n- **Fix**: Changed `toxicityMetric` to only accept the `outputs` parameter and always use `defaultBannedTerms`. This prevents the references array from being misinterpreted.\n\nBoth fixes maintain backward compatibility:\n- Existing code using default exports continues to work\n- The toxicityMetric function signature change doesn't break any call sites since it was only used through `DEFAULT_METRICS` in the test suite\n\nThe test suite now passes with all 28 tests successful across 8 test files.",
